{"question": "What unusual condition characterizes the Ice Truck Killer's victims?", "keywords": ["victims", "bloodless", "dismemberment"], "reference_answer": "The victims are dismembered and drained of blood, with the body parts arranged in deliberate displays.", "source_chapter": 3, "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "Which musical composer does Dexter listen to while examining photographs?", "keywords": ["Philip Glass", "CD", "photographs"], "reference_answer": "Dexter puts on a Philip Glass CD while examining the photographs on his computer.", "source_chapter": 13, "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "What is the name of the priest Dexter watches at the beginning of the novel?", "keywords": ["Father Donovan", "priest"], "reference_answer": "The priest is Father Donovan.", "source_chapter": 1, "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "What is Dexter's internal name for the force or presence associated with his murderous urges?", "keywords": ["Dark Passenger", "Need"], "reference_answer": "Dexter calls it the Dark Passenger, an internal presence associated with his violent urges.", "source_chapter": 1, "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "Who is the detective who becomes suspicious of Dexter?", "keywords": ["Sergeant Doakes", "suspicion", "Dexter"], "reference_answer": "Sergeant James Doakes becomes suspicious of Dexter.", "source_chapter": [3, 8, 12], "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "What is the name of Dexter's forensic colleague who reacts to the displayed heads?", "keywords": ["Vince Masuoka", "heads", "crime scene"], "reference_answer": "Vince Masuoka is the colleague who asks Dexter where the bodies are when they examine the display of heads.", "source_chapter": 3, "category": "direct_fact"}
# {"question": "Which police lieutenant manages important parts of the murder investigation?", "keywords": ["LaGuerta", "lieutenant", "investigation"], "reference_answer": "Lieutenant Maria LaGuerta is a senior officer involved in the investigation.", "source_chapter": 3, "category": "direct_fact"}
