{"question": "How does the novel contrast outward normality with inner reality?", "keywords": ["Dexter", "Dark Passenger", "Rita"], "reference_answer": "Dexter performs the role of a conventional employee and partner while concealing the violent urges and private thoughts that shape his internal life.", "source_chapter": [1, 6, 16, 17], "category": "thematic_analysis"}
{"question": "How does the idea of artistry complicate the novel's portrayal of violence?", "keywords": ["crime scene", "Dexter", "killer"], "reference_answer": "Dexter's response to the staged displays shows how he can perceive composition and skill in acts that are horrifying to others. The contrast complicates the distinction between aesthetic appreciation and moral judgment.", "source_chapter": [3, 11, 20], "category": "thematic_analysis"}
